    "title": "Mississippi State flips former Stanford commit, 3-star 2027 LB - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ethan Stone ,\n1 days ago Mississippi State scored a big recruiting win on Monday night, landing a pledge from former Stanford commit Devontray Brewer. The 3-star linebacker prospect originally committed to Stanford on June 2 and flipped following an official visit to Starkville on June 19. Brewer hails from Tupelo high school in Tupelo, Mississippi and stands at 6-foot-1, 225 pounds. In addition to Mississippi State and Stanford, Brewer also held offers from Michigan, Ole Miss and Arkansas, to name a few. “There’s no better ball than the SEC, so this is an honor and privilege to be able to play in the league and... Read full article\n1",
